The user wants to "Treat whitespace-only values as invalid." In the code, currently isValid checks length > 0. That would treat whitespace-only strings as valid because length > 0 (e.g., "   " length 3). The request wants to treat whitespace-only values as invalid, meaning isValid should return false if string trimmed is empty. So need to change isValid in src/customerValidator.ts (focused) to check if trimmed length > 0, i.e., return value.trim().length > 0. Could also check (value.trim() !== ""). Equivalent.

Thus we propose patch for src/customerValidator.ts. Need to replace the function body (or entire function). Let's locate existing function:

```
export function isValid(value: string) {
  return value.length > 0;
}
```

We need to modify to:

```
export function isValid(value: string) {
  return value.trim().length > 0;
}
```

We should keep same formatting.

Thus propose patch with summary: Update isValid to treat whitespace-only strings as invalid by trimming.

Now produce propose_patch.

